From c6fb0025a60c33af289d4f39962fa81190f4da0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:34:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] cron: wait out a claim's admission.lock hold; a
 still-busy lock defers the tick (N3)

With the hub CPU gate on (#778), a Kanban claim holds admission.lock for ~1-2.25 s
(CLAIM_MAX_HOLD_S). cron's tick reserved with one 50 ms try and, since AdmissionBusy is a
TimeoutError, failed OPEN: it dispatched with no reservation and without checking the hold, and
the run's own extend() failed the same way. The run was then invisible to hermes-sync's drain
(the t_01a189db034f3b2b class: restart held open past the window / restart on old code).

- admission_fence.reserve()/extend() take an optional timeout (default unchanged 0.05 s for
  callers holding the session-map lock).
- cron's update_admission() and _take_run_reservation() hold no session lock: they pass
  backend_retirement.BUSY_WAIT_S (CLAIM_MAX_HOLD_S + 0.5). No turn-waiter marker is registered,
  so claims do not defer to cron.
- A lock still busy after that wait yields False (dispatch nothing, advance nothing; due jobs
  fire once on a later tick). Any other OSError (unwritable root) still fails open.

Problem: probe (real flock, separate process) - a 1.5 s lock holder made the tick admit with 0
  reservation files after 0.052 s.
Why 1: update_admission() caught (OSError, TimeoutError) and yielded True - cron/scheduler_tick.py.
Why 2: reserve() hard-codes a 50 ms try, sized for callers holding the session-map lock.
Why 3: #778 made multi-second lock holds normal (full CPU sample under the lock) without
  revisiting lock-free callers that used the short try.
Root (happened): one fixed timeout for all reserve() callers; busy and unavailable were handled
  by one fail-open branch.
Root (not caught): cron admission tests covered hold and lock-free cases only, no real-process
  lock holder. Countermeasure: the real-process tests below.

Tests (RED on bd18747d7e0, GREEN here):
- tests/cron/test_update_admission_hold.py: 1.5 s holder -> tick waits, dispatches with >= 1
  reservation, no turn-waiter; holder > BUSY_WAIT_S -> tick returns 0, no dispatch/advance, then
  fires once after release; run reservation waits out a 1.5 s holder; unwritable root still
  fails open.
- tests/hermes_cli/test_admission_fence.py: reserve/extend default stay one short try; timeout=
  waits.

Card: t_01a1a375eb4f4c4c (delta review t_01a1a3679692b3c2). Stacked on #778 (reviewed head bd18747d7e0; now d8cdddffb45, which touches none of these files).
---
